          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On August 5, 2010 at 10:55 PM, during a summer walk, the witness spotted a bright yellow sphere moving in a north-south trajectory above the city at a moderate speed. This peculiar case (a glowing point moving in a straight line) has low consistency due to the imprecision of the orientation and the description of the phenomenon itself (vague apparent size). The hypothesis of observing a large satellite remains the most probable, but it is not proven. This case is classified C due to lack of information and the noted imprecision.",
